From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: leak REO queue descriptor when its cache flush fails

ath12k_dp_reo_cmd_free() freed the REO queue descriptor even when the
HAL_REO_CMD_FLUSH_CACHE command had failed. REO may still hold the
descriptor in its cache and write it back later, into whatever object
reuses the memory (kmalloc-2k, shared with netlink sockets). Leak the
descriptor instead and say so in the (ratelimited) warning.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -408,9 +408,16 @@ void ath12k_dp_reo_cmd_free(struct ath12k_dp *dp, void *ctx,
 {
 	struct ath12k_dp_rx_tid_rxq *rx_tid = ctx;
 
-	if (status != HAL_REO_CMD_SUCCESS)
-		ath12k_warn(dp->ab, "failed to flush rx tid hw desc, tid %d status %d\n",
-			    rx_tid->tid, status);
+	if (status != HAL_REO_CMD_SUCCESS) {
+		/* REO may still hold this descriptor in its cache and write
+		 * it back later. Freeing it would let that write land in
+		 * whatever object reuses the memory, so leak it instead.
+		 */
+		ath12k_warn(dp->ab,
+			    "failed to flush rx tid %d hw desc, status %d: leaking %u byte descriptor\n",
+			    rx_tid->tid, status, rx_tid->qbuf.size);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	ath12k_dp_rx_tid_cleanup(dp->ab, &rx_tid->qbuf);
 }
